WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.422
Your video is only half the job on YouTube.

2
00:00:03.472 --> 00:00:09.437
The title, description, chapters and thumbnail decide whether anyone finds it, and whether they stay.

3
00:00:10.437 --> 00:00:14.440
Before uploading, export an MP4 and watch it all the way through.

4
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.666
Catch typos and internal information, and jot down when each new section starts.

5
00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:24.634
A good title says what viewers will learn, in the words they'd type.

6
00:00:24.684 --> 00:00:29.663
So Q4 Webinar becomes How to Plan a Q4 Marketing Budget for a Small Business.

7
00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:35.267
Make the first two lines a plain summary, since they show before the more link.

8
00:00:35.317 --> 00:00:39.007
Then add three to five bullets, your chapters and your links.

9
00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:44.313
List timestamps starting at zero, one per line with a title.

10
00:00:44.363 --> 00:00:49.284
Your section divider slides and point-making headlines become ready-made chapter titles.

11
00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:54.787
Your slide headlines and speaker notes give you the chapters and description.

12
00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:59.038
On Pro, AI directs your deck into a video that holds viewers.

13
00:00:59.088 --> 00:01:02.267
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

